{"name":"Blowout","hex":"#658499","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blowout","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sudden puncturing of a pneumatic tyre/tire.","A sudden release of oil and gas from a well."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blowout"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blowout (well drilling)","blocks":[{"text":"A blowout is the uncontrolled release of crude oil and/or natural gas from an oil well or gas well after pressure control systems have failed. Modern wells have blowout preventers intended to prevent such an occurrence. An accidental spark during a blowout can lead to a catastrophic oil or gas fire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Lucas_gusher.jpg/330px-Lucas_gusher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blowout_(well_drilling)","wikidata":"Q885506"},{"title":"Blowout (tire)","blocks":[{"text":"A blowout is a rapid, explosive loss of inflation pressure of a pneumatic tire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Tireimpactdamage.jpg/330px-Tireimpactdamage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blowout_(tire)","wikidata":"Q4928622"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Lucas_gusher.jpg/500px-Lucas_gusher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Lucas_gusher.jpg/1280px-Lucas_gusher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Lucas_gusher.jpg/500px-Lucas_gusher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Lucas Gusher at Spindletop, Texas (1901)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALucas_gusher.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wik